    "# Phase 1 - Local Ollama Multi-Model Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "All models are called through the same `ChatOllama` interface so that model identity is the experimental factor while prompts and cascade mechanics stay constant.\n",
    "\n",
    "`llama3.2:latest` is treated separately as a scale check because it belongs to the same Llama family as the core model.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Define the local Ollama language models used as the decision engines for the simulated agents.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this phase does**\n",
    "- Defines the core model, architecture-comparison models, and the larger same-family scale-check model.\n",
    "- Uses the same local Ollama endpoint so model comparisons use a common interface.\n",
    "- Provides an optional connection test before expensive simulations begin.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main outputs.** `CORE_MODEL`, `ARCHITECTURE_MODELS`, `SCALE_CHECK_MODEL`, `ALL_MODELS`, and model connection status.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run note.** Ollama must be running locally and the required models must already be pulled. A failed connection test should be fixed before Phase 8 is started.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b95e7643",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Ollama model roles\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell assigns different experimental roles to the local models.\n",
    "\n",
    "- The **core model** supports the full Stage A experiment.\n",
    "- The **architecture models** support cross-model robustness.\n",
    "- The **scale-check model** supports the focused Stage D same-family comparison.\n",
    "\n",
    "Keeping these roles explicit prevents accidental mixing of core and robustness conditions.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "4dc1d349",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Configured models:\n",
      "  llama3.2:1b          INSTALLED\n",
      "  gemma3:latest        INSTALLED\n",
      "  qwen2.5-coder:7b     INSTALLED\n",
      "  llama3.2:latest      INSTALLED\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "OLLAMA_BASE_URL = \"http://localhost:11434\"\n",
    "\n",
    "ARCHITECTURE_MODELS = [\n",
    "    \"llama3.2:1b\",\n",
    "    \"gemma3:latest\",\n",
    "    \"qwen2.5-coder:7b\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "SCALE_CHECK_MODEL = \"llama3.2:latest\"\n",
    "\n",
    "ALL_MODELS = ARCHITECTURE_MODELS + [SCALE_CHECK_MODEL]\n",
    "CORE_MODEL = \"llama3.2:1b\"\n",
    "\n",
    "LLM_TEMPERATURE = 0.30\n",
    "MAX_RETRIES = 4\n",
    "RETRY_BASE_DELAY = 2.0\n",
    "\n",
    "_MODEL_CACHE = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "def get_llm(model_name: str, temperature: float = LLM_TEMPERATURE) -> ChatOllama:\n",
    "    key = (model_name, float(temperature))\n",
    "    if key not in _MODEL_CACHE:\n",
    "        _MODEL_CACHE[key] = ChatOllama(\n",
    "            model=model_name,\n",
    "            temperature=temperature,\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    return _MODEL_CACHE[key]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def get_installed_ollama_models():\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        response = requests.get(\n",
    "            f\"{OLLAMA_BASE_URL}/api/tags\",\n",
    "            timeout=10\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "        return [\n",
    "            item.get(\"name\", \"\")\n",
    "            for item in response.json().get(\"models\", [])\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    except Exception as exc:\n",
    "        print(\"Could not connect to Ollama:\", exc)\n",
    "        return []\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "installed_ollama_models = get_installed_ollama_models()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Configured models:\")\n",
    "for model in ALL_MODELS:\n",
    "    status = \"INSTALLED\" if model in installed_ollama_models else \"NOT DETECTED\"\n",
    "    print(f\"  {model:20} {status}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if not installed_ollama_models:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nStart Ollama before running LLM simulations.\")"
   ]
