    "# Phase 2 - Build 100 Heterogeneous Agents\n",
    "\n",
    "Agents contain demographics, political leaning, Big Five traits, trust, scepticism and digital literacy.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same deterministic population is reused for a given population condition across replications and model comparisons. This makes model comparisons fairer and makes the Agent-ID random effect meaningful in the later mixed-effects model.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Construct the heterogeneous population that gives the experiment its psychological and demographic variation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this phase does**\n",
    "- Creates 100 agents with demographic characteristics.\n",
    "- Assigns Big Five personality traits.\n",
    "- Adds trust, scepticism, and digital-literacy attributes.\n",
    "- Creates population conditions in which selected traits are elevated while other traits remain near the baseline distribution.\n",
    "- Converts each structured agent profile into a natural-language system prompt for the LLM.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main outputs.** Reusable agent populations and system prompts that condition LLM behaviour.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation note.** Personality does not deterministically force an action. It is supplied to the LLM as behavioural context, allowing the model to decide among the available actions.\n"
   ]
  },
