    "# Phase 3 - Build Multiple Social-Network Topologies\n",
    "\n",
    "The experiment uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Barabási–Albert scale-free network\n",
    "- Erdős–Rényi random network\n",
    "- Watts–Strogatz small-world network\n",
    "\n",
    "Average degree is kept broadly comparable across the three structures.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Represent the social environment in which information can move from one agent to another.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this phase does**\n",
    "- Builds a Barabási–Albert scale-free network for the core experiment.\n",
    "- Builds Erdős–Rényi and Watts–Strogatz alternatives for robustness analysis.\n",
    "- Uses 100 nodes so each network corresponds directly to the 100 simulated agents.\n",
    "- Produces a visual comparison of the network structures.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main outputs.** `NETWORK_GRAPHS`, topology names, network summary information, and the topology comparison figure.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Research role.** Holding the scale-free topology fixed in Stage A isolates the primary personality/information effects; Stage C tests whether conclusions change under alternative network structures.\n"
   ]
  },
