    "# Phase 8 - Full Experimental Design and Execution\n",
    "\n",
    "The expensive experiment is staged rather than forcing a full Cartesian product across every factor.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Stage A - Main confirmatory experiment\n",
    "Core model × core topology × all 6 populations × all 6 stimuli × **30 replications**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Stage B - Cross-model robustness\n",
    "Three architecture-diverse local models × selected populations/stimuli × core topology × **30 replications**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Stage C - Network-topology robustness\n",
    "Core model × all three topologies × selected populations/stimuli × **30 replications**.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Stage D - Same-family scale check\n",
    "`llama3.2:latest` repeats the focused robustness subset at the core topology.\n",
    "\n",
    "Every completed run is appended immediately to a checkpoint CSV. Re-running a stage skips completed run IDs.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Define and execute the complete staged experimental design.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Experimental structure**\n",
    "- **Stage A - Core:** core model × scale-free topology × all six populations × all six stimuli × 30 replications = **1,080 runs**.\n",
    "- **Stage B - Model robustness:** comparator architectures on a reduced common subset = **540 runs**.\n",
    "- **Stage C - Topology robustness:** alternative network topologies on the same reduced subset = **540 runs**.\n",
    "- **Stage D - Scale check:** larger same-family model on a focused subset = **120 runs**.\n",
    "- **Total planned runs = 2,280.**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why stages are used.** A full Cartesian product across every model, topology, population, stimulus, and replication would be unnecessarily expensive. The staged design keeps the main factorial test comprehensive while using matched subsets for robustness checks.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main outputs.** Checkpoint CSV files for cascade histories and agent decisions, plus combined Phase 8 datasets.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run note.** If the experiments have already been completed and you only want to redo the analysis, set the four `RUN_STAGE_*` switches to `False`. Existing checkpoint files can still be combined and analysed.\n"
   ]
  },
