    "# Phase 14 - Main Confirmatory ANOVA\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses only Stage A so that model/topology robustness stages do not confound the primary population × information analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Test the primary factorial hypotheses using only the controlled Stage A core experiment.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Model.** Two-way ANOVA on the core run-level data tests:\n",
    "1. the main effect of population personality composition;\n",
    "2. the main effect of information type; and\n",
    "3. the population × information-type interaction.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why only Stage A?** Model and topology robustness runs deliberately use reduced subsets. Mixing them into the main ANOVA would unbalance and confound the confirmatory design.\n",
    "\n",
