    "# Phase 21 - Generalised Linear Mixed-Effects Model\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Outcome: whether an exposed agent **shared**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Fixed effects include Big Five traits, behavioural attributes, information veracity, model and topology.\n",
    "\n",
    "Random intercepts:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `simulation_run`\n",
    "- `agent_cluster_id`\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Correct the pseudoreplication problem that arises when thousands of agent decisions are treated as independent observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Model structure**\n",
    "- Binary outcome: whether an exposed agent shared.\n",
    "- Fixed effects: available Big Five traits, trust/scepticism/digital literacy, information type, model, and topology.\n",
    "- Interaction: conscientiousness × information type.\n",
    "- Random intercepts: simulation run and agent cluster.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Implementation.** The notebook uses `BinomialBayesMixedGLM` with variational-Bayes fitting and reports approximate fixed-effect odds ratios and significance statistics.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main outputs.** `GLMM_FITTED`, `glmm_results_table`, a saved fixed-effects CSV, and a model summary text file.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run note.** Do not manually set `GLMM_FITTED = True`. It should become `True` only after the fitting code succeeds on the cleaned agent-level dataset.\n"
   ]
  },
