    "# Phase 26 - Cascade Timing and Reach Thresholds\n",
    "\n",
    "### Phase Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose.** Describe not only how large cascades become, but how quickly they reach important levels of exposure.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this phase does**\n",
    "- Summarises available time-to-threshold variables such as 25%, 50%, and 75% reach.\n",
    "- Compares timing measures across experimental conditions.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main output.** `timing_summary_df`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation.** Timing measures complement final cascade size: two cascades can reach similar sizes while spreading at very different speeds.\n"
   ]
  },
